# counter harness. One force call is one GMIN potential request to lennard_jones.
# The binary was built from the Wales tarball named by commit. The pin is that sha256.
# energy is the lowest quench at or below SLOPPYCONV. lowest_energy on each start is the lowest finite evaluation.
# Serial basin-hopping with the archived lj98 symmetrise moves. One replica at temperature 1.3. BHPT is unset, so the MPI temperature reset keeps TEMPERATURE 1.3. Quenches are L-BFGS with SLOPPYCONV 0.007, TIGHTCONV 1.0e-5, and MAXIT 1000 and 1000. STEP is 0.46 and ASTEP is 0.47. FIXBOTH, PERMDIST 0.01, NEWRESTART 6, SORT, SAVE 1, and SYMMETRISE 1 0.01 0.05 0.3 0.1 0.6 3 0.3 2.1 are the archive data file. STEPS is 100000 1.0. The archive sets no RADIUS and no RANSEED. RADIUS is omitted and the coordinates are not translated before CENTRE. The cap and MAX_NPCALL are problems/globalopt/lj98.toml convergence.max_force_calls, 1000000000. EDIFF is 0.001, the problem energy_above_minimum. TARGET is the harness energy of codes/gmin/reference/lj98.points. The data file starts with MPI because the binary is the MPI build, and mpirun launches it. Starts are the 100 numbered coords files. The unnumbered coords file is not a start. A start that already succeeded keeps its call count.
